<script lang="ts">import { onMount } from 'svelte';import { api } from '$lib/api';let status=$state<any>(null),error=$state(''),updated=$state('');const stateLabel=(state:string)=>({open:'Available',checking:'Being checked',complete:'Complete',validation_error:'Check failed',delivery_exhausted:'Needs owner review',importing:'Being imported'}[state]??state.replaceAll('_',' '));async function refresh(){try{status=await api('status');updated=new Date().toLocaleTimeString();error='';}catch(e){error=e instanceof Error?e.message:'Status is unavailable.';}}onMount(()=>{void refresh();const timer=setInterval(refresh,60000);return()=>clearInterval(timer);});</script>
<svelte:head><title>Operating status — Voynich@home</title><meta name="description" content="Check whether Voynich@home assignments are open and review the remaining public-release checks."/></svelte:head>
<div class="page narrow"><p class="eyebrow">Development preview</p><h1>Assignments and release status</h1><p class="lede">Campaigns stop assigning tasks when their work is complete. New computation begins only under a published campaign or continuation.</p>{#if error}<p class="error" role="alert">{error}</p>{/if}
<section class="panel"><h2>{status?status.assignments_enabled?'Work assignments are open':'No new work is available':'Checking for available work…'}</h2><p>{status?.reason??'Contacting the project server.'}</p><p class="small muted">Deployment stage: {status?.stage??'unavailable'} · Last checked: {updated||'waiting for response'}</p><button class="secondary" onclick={refresh}>Refresh status</button></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>Work queue</h2>{#if status?.queue?.length}<table><thead><tr><th>State</th><th>Tasks</th></tr></thead><tbody>{#each status.queue as q}<tr><td>{stateLabel(q.state)}</td><td>{q.count}</td></tr>{/each}</tbody></table>{:else}<p class="muted">No tasks have been published.</p>{/if}</section>
<section class="panel"><h2>Checks required before public release</h2><p>Local queue checks have passed. The remaining checks cover:</p><ul><li>Hosted task recovery and browser resource controls.</li><li>Google and GitHub account integration.</li><li>Restoration from a hosted backup.</li><li>Release rollback in the hosted environment.</li></ul><a href="https://github.com/javidmardanov/VoynichAtHome/blob/33debe761229e99816cd6d0f1efc1bc65c775b4d/docs/RELEASE-STATUS.md">Review the evidence for each release check ↗</a></section>
<details><summary>Operating budget</summary><p class="small muted">The initial target is $10 per month. Before assigning a task, the server reserves enough capacity to check its result. Application limits reduce exposure but do not impose a spending cap at the hosting provider.</p></details></div>
